Next, local processing can be faster since there's no latency from the cloud. So, things like instant voice commands or real-time object detection. But wait, the user wants 25 items, so I need to think of different categories. Maybe security features, like biometric authentication. That's a good one because cloud-based systems might have vulnerabilities.

Also, low-latency applications, like gaming or AR where quick responses are needed. Then, offline functionality, like using apps without internet. Maybe predictive text that's trained on the user's own data, not a cloud model. That's different.

